  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "If $\\,\\text{Re}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\text{Im}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ d\\end{aligned}]\\,$ are the real and imaginary parts of the vector $\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-4+9\\text{i} \\\\ 1+8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ then what is the value of $bc-ad?$",
  "worked_solution": "For the given vector $\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-4+9\\text{i} \\\\ 1+8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =[\\begin{aligned}-4+9\\text{i} \\\\ 1+8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{\u23df}}_{\\text{Re}(x)}+\\text{i}\\,{{[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]}_{\u23df}}_{\\text{Im}(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $\\,a=-4,b=1,c=9$ and $d=8$, which implies that \n\n$$\nbc-ad=1\\cdot 9-(-4)\\cdot 8=41.\n$$",
